	url = {https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105033826298?origin=resultslist},
	affiliations = {Physics Department, St. Xavier’s College, Mumbai, 400001, India},
	abstract = {The study aims to validate the hydrostatic equation using a low-cost, Arduino-based pressure measurement system. An Arduino microcontroller was integrated with a BMP280 sensor and LCD display to collect atmospheric pressure and altitude data across different floor levels of a multi-story building. The system included a push-button interface for automated pressure logging at regular intervals. Theoretical pressure values were calculated using the barometric formula, assuming an isothermal atmosphere, and were compared with the measured data. The results showed strong agreement with theoretical results. Minor deviations were observed due to sensor limitations, temperature gradients, and environmental influences. Overall, the experiment demonstrates that such a microcontroller-based system is effective for verifying the hydrostatic principle and holds significant potential for educational use and small-scale environmental monitoring. © 2025 IOP Publishing Ltd. All rights, including for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies, are reserved.},
