	abstract = {We discuss an in-class activity for introductory mechanics students to examine the forces on an airplane and the resulting path at takeoff using Excel and VLC Player. We use a Euler-based integration method within Excel to predict the takeoff run for a Boeing 747-400 ERF considering forces such as thrust, lift, drag, and friction. We then used VLC Player to analyse a YouTube video of a Boeing 747-400 ERF at takeoff to measure take-off times, distances, velocities, and accelerations. We then compare these data with the predictions. Particularly when the effects of friction are included, the data match the predicted values well for distances and velocities, but the discrepancies are significantly larger for the accelerations, suggesting that a more complex model is required (such as velocity dependence of thrust). We include a video, the detailed instructions for this exercise, and the Excel code as supplementary materials. © 2024 The Author(s). Published by IOP Publishing Ltd.},
