	affiliations = {Department of Physics Education, Farhangian University, PO Box 14665-889, Tehran, Iran},
	abstract = {This study evaluates the effectiveness of the STEAM (Science, Technology, Engineering, Arts, and Mathematics)-integrated project-based learning (PJBL-STEAM) model in enhancing problem-solving abilities and conceptual understanding among seventh-grade students studying the topic of density. A quasi-experimental design with pre-test and post-test assessments was employed, involving an experimental group (PJBL-STEAM) and a control group (traditional instruction). The population consisted of seventh-grade students from Mosleynejad Girls’ High School in Mashhad, Iran, during the 2023–2024 academic years. A sample of 30 students (15 per group) was selected using cluster random sampling. Both groups participated in the pre-test, post-test, and retention test. Data were collected via a researcher-made questionnaire, validated by physics professors, with a Cronbach’s alpha reliability of 0.759. The experimental group underwent four 90 min PJBL-STEAM sessions, while the control group received traditional instruction. Post-test results indicated a significant improvement in problem-solving abilities and conceptual understanding in the experimental group compared to the control group (p < 0.05). A retention test conducted six months later revealed a significant difference (t (28) = 3.79, p < 0.01), indicating that the experimental group maintained superior performance over time. The PJBL-STEAM approach fostered active engagement, creativity and conceptual understanding of density. These findings suggest that PJBL-STEAM is an effective method for teaching abstract physics concepts and enhancing problem-solving skills student. Recommendations include broader adoption of PJBL-STEAM in science education to develop 21st-century skills. © 2026 IOP Publishing Ltd. All rights, including for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies, are reserved. This article is available under the terms of the IOP-Standard License.},
