	affiliations = {Kiel Univ., Germany},
	abstract = {Steadily increasing developments in the natural sciences and increasingly complex procedures and apparatus are making it extremely difficult for traditional forms of instruction to equip the next generation with either an understanding of the problems it will have to face or a willingness to work together on these. This inability to cope with the situation can be attributed to insufficient coordination of instruction in the individual subjects and to the limited amount of specialised knowledge imparted. The author therefore advocates an integrated course of instruction for the natural sciences which, by encompassing central topics, is designed not only to impart knowledge but also to give students the opportunity to develop fundamental insights. These insights make general interrelationships between the natural sciences accessible to the students and serve as points of reference in the students' later lives.},
